saw announcements about agent swarms and new model economics.\",\n    31→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n    32→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog\",\n    33→    \"date\": \"2026-07-10\",\n    34→    \"community_feedback\": [\n    35→      {\n    36→        \"quote\": \"The Cursor people concluded their last post with 'taste, judgement, and direction came from humans'. Sounded surprisingly sane after 'don't trust humans' messaging from competitors.\",\n    37→        \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    38→        \"sentiment\": \"neutral\"\n    39→      },\n    40→      {\n    41→        \"quote\": \"Cursor had a good attitude toward AI coding agents initially but seemed to be abandoning that approach, possibly to appease investors.\",\n    42→        \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    43→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n    44→      }\n    45→    ]\n    46→  },\n    47→  {\n    48→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n    49→    \"title\": \"Enhanced Code Review Customization and New Models\",\n    50→    \"description\": \"GitHub improved Copilot code review with more customization and control, adding head-branch custom instructions and broader instruction file support. Visual Studio update on July 14 focused on visibility and trust with clearer usage insights. Gemini 3.6 Flash became available in GitHub Copilot.\",\n    51→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    52→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/\",\n    53→    \"date\": \"2026-07-14\",\n    54→    \"community_feedback\": [\n    55→      {\n    56→        \"quote\": \"Strong negative sentiment regarding the pricing model changes. Users questioning if the new costs are sustainable.\",\n    57→        \"source\": \"Reddit - r/GithubCopilot\",\n    58→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n    59→      },\n    60→      {\n    61→        \"quote\": \"Concerns about the false messaging around community resonance with the changes\",\n    62→        \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    63→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n    64→      }\n    65→    ]\n    66→  },\n    67→  {\n    68→    \"productName\": \"Windsurf\",\n    69→    \"title\": \"Agent Skills for Cascade and UI Updates\",\n    70→    \"description\": \"Windsurf (Codeium's AI-native IDE) released support for Agent Skills for Cascade in July 2026. Updates included ACU usage display, smoother Windows setup, faster MCP startup times, subagent default models configuration, and a new app icon/wordmark branding.\",\n    71→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    72→    \"url\": \"https://docs.devin.ai/desktop/changelog\",\n    73→    \"date\": \"2026-07-15\",\n    74→    \"community_feedback\": [\n    75→      {\n    76→        \"quote\": \"Windsurf is a '$3B dev-focused acquisition to level up AI coding workflows'. Positioned as a Cursor alternative for developers already using Codeium.\",\n    77→        \"source\": \"Facebook tech groups\",\n    78→        \"sentiment\": \"neutral\"\n    79→      },\n    80→      {\n    81→        \"quote\": \"Free for July 2026 access with promotional code '20July261mth'\",\n    82→        \"source\": \"Social media promotions\",\n    83→        \"sentiment\": \"positive\"\n    84→      }\n    85→    ]\n    86→  },\n    87→  {\n    88→    \"productName\": \"Devin\",\n    89→    \"title\": \"Desktop App v2026.5.26 and Cascade Hooks\",\n    90→    \"description\": \"Devin released Desktop Application v2026.5.26 on July 15, 2026, with bundled Devin Local agent. New features include Cascade Hooks (available to all tiers), enhanced autonomous coding workflows, auto-triage features, and 3× faster startup. Classic machine configuration available as read-only until July 31, 2026.\",\n    91→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n    92→    \"url\": \"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\",\n    93→    \"date\": \"2026-07-15\",\n    94→    \"community_feedback\": [\n    95→      {\n    96→        \"quote\": \"After 7 days of testing, it's not here to replace programmers - it's the ultimate productivity booster\",\n    97→        \"source\": \"Independent reviewer\",\n    98→        \"sentiment\": \"positive\"\n    99→      },\n   100→      {\n   101→        \"quote\": \"Devin framed as a useful 'code monkey' for specific tasks that can be accomplished with minimal or no external context\",\n   102→        \"source\": \"FreeCodeCamp Forum\",\n   103→        \"sentiment\": \"neutral\"\n   104→      }\n   105→    ]\n   106→  },\n   107→  {\n   108→    \"productName\": \"Continue\",\n   109→    \"title\": \"Continue.dev Acquired by Cursor - Shutdown Announcement\",\n   110→    \"description\": \"Continue.dev was acquired by Cursor and announced shutdown. All user data to be permanently deleted from Continue's servers on July 15, 2026. Recent features before shutdown included enhanced image support in CLI, improved CLI messaging, shell mode, and safety improvements.\",\n   111→    \"updateType\": \"announcement\",\n   112→    \"url\": \"https://changelog.continue.dev/\",\n   113→    \"date\": \"2026-07-01\",\n   114→    \"community_feedback\": [\n   115→      {\n   116→        \"quote\": \"Continue was 'the cleanest open-source bet in AI coding in 2026' with Apache 2.0 licensing and pluggable provider support\",\n   117→        \"source\": \"Industry analysis\",\n   118→        \"sentiment\": \"positive\"\n   119→      }\n   120→    ]\n   121→  },\n   122→  {\n   123→    \"productName\": \"Codex CLI\",\n   124→    \"title\": \"OpenAI Codex CLI July 2026 Updates\",\n   125→    \"description\": \"OpenAI released Codex CLI updates throughout July 2026, including experimental paginated thread history, efficient resume and search capabilities, persisted names support, sub-agent support, and memory features. ChatGPT Desktop received experience updates on July 16.\",\n   126→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   127→    \"url\": \"https://github.com/openai/codex/releases\",\n   128→    \"date\": \"2026-07-16\",\n   129→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   130→  },\n   131→  {\n   132→    \"productName\": \"Gemini CLI\",\n   133→    \"title\": \"v0.50.0 Stable Release and Preview v0.51.0\",\n   134→    \"description\": \"Google released Gemini CLI v0.50.0 stable on July 8, 2026, with new commands (/agents refresh, /skills reload) and enhanced release verification. v0.51.0-preview.0 also released same day with experimental features. Nightly builds include v0.52.0-nightly.20260715 with core and a2a fixes.\",\n   135→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n   136→    \"url\": \"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\",\n   137→    \"date\": \"2026-07-08\",\n   138→    \"community_feedback\": [\n   139→      {\n   140→        \"quote\": \"Complaints about Gemini CLI performance and reliability issues, with discussions about the '2026 Stability Crisis'\",\n   141→        \"source\": \"Google AI Developer Forum\",\n   142→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n   143→      },\n   144→      {\n   145→        \"quote\": \"Gemini-CLI is unusable with numerous untriaged issues\",\n   146→        \"source\": \"GitHub Discussions #25448\",\n   147→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n   148→      },\n   149→      {\n   150→        \"quote\": \"Article titled 'Google Quietly Killed Gemini CLI' discussing the discontinuation\",\n   151→        \"source\": \"Dev.to\",\n   152→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n   153→      }\n   154→    ]\n   155→  }\n   156→]\n   157→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
