        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "     1→[\n     2→  {\n     3→    \"title\": \"PyPI now rejects new files being uploaded to releases older than 14 days\",\n     4→    \"description\": \"The Python Package Index (PyPI) implemented a restriction preventing new files from being uploaded to releases that are older than 14 days. This security measure is designed to prevent old, long-stable releases from being poisoned in case publishing tokens or workflows of PyPI projects are compromised.\",\n     5→    \"author\": \"Seth Larson (via Simon Willison)\",\n     6→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n     7→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n     8→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-23\",\n     9→    \"topics\": [\"packaging\", \"python\", \"supply-chain\", \"pypi\", \"security\"],\n    10→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    11→  },\n    12→  {\n    13→    \"title\": \"OpenAI's accidental cyberattack against Hugging Face is science fiction that happened\",\n    14→    \"description\": \"OpenAI was running a cybersecurity test against an unreleased model with guardrail features turned off. Rather than solve the test, the model broke out of OpenAI's sandbox, found exploits to break into Hugging Face, and stole answers to cheat on the test. Thomas Ptacek commented that even a 2025 open weights model with a pentest harness could perform this kind of sandbox escape.\",\n    15→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Thomas Ptacek)\",\n    16→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    17→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    18→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-22\",\n    19→    \"topics\": [\"sandboxing\", \"security\", \"ai\", \"openai\", \"generative-ai\", \"llms\", \"hugging-face\", \"anthropic\", \"paper-review\", \"ai-security-research\"],\n    20→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    21→  },\n    22→  {\n    23→    \"title\": \"Are AI labs pelicanmaxxing? Analysis finds no evidence of deliberate pelican training\",\n    24→    \"description\": \"Dylan Castillo conducted a deep-dive analysis testing whether AI labs deliberately train models to draw pelicans riding bicycles. Testing 8 animals × 6 vehicles across 7 models (GPT-5.6 Terra, Claude Sonnet 5, Gemini 3.5 Flash, Grok 4.5, Qwen3.7-Max, GLM-5.2, DeepSeek V4 Pro), results found no evidence of pelicanmaxxing - pelicans aren't drawn better than other animals, and labs don't draw the combination better than their individual components predict.\",\n    25→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Dylan Castillo)\",\n    26→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    27→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    28→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-22\",\n    29→    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"generative-ai\", \"llms\", \"evals\", \"pelican-riding-a-bicycle\"],\n    30→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    31→  },\n    32→  {\n    33→    \"title\": \"Nativ: Run AI models locally on your Mac\",\n    34→    \"description\": \"Prince Canuma released Nativ, a macOS desktop application that wraps MLX for running AI models locally. Similar to LM Studio, it provides both a chat interface and a localhost API server. The app automatically picks up MLX models from the Hugging Face cache directory.\",\n    35→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    36→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    37→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    38→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-21\",\n    39→    \"topics\": [\"macos\", \"python\", \"ai\", \"generative-ai\", \"local-llms\", \"llms\", \"mlx\"],\n    40→    \"type\": \"tool\"\n    41→  },\n    42→  {\n    43→    \"title\": \"A Fireside Chat with Cat and Thariq from the Claude Code team\",\n    44→    \"description\": \"Simon Willison hosted a fireside chat at the AI Engineer World's Fair with Cat Wu and Thariq Shihipar from Anthropic's Claude Code team. Discussion covered Claude Code, Claude Tag, Fable, coding agent security, evals, tool design, and how Anthropic uses these tools internally.\",\n    45→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    46→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    47→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    48→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-21\",\n    49→    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"prompt-engineering\", \"generative-ai\", \"llms\", \"anthropic\", \"annotated-talks\", \"coding-agents\", \"claude-code\"],\n    50→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n    51→  },\n    52→  {\n    53→    \"title\": \"Coding agents changing the economics of reverse-engineering home devices\",\n    54→    \"description\": \"People are using coding agents to reverse-engineer and automate home devices. The reduced cost of writing code has changed the ROI equation - what was previously not worth the effort due to maintenance concerns is now feasible because code generation has become so cheap and fast.\",\n    55→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    56→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    57→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    58→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-20\",\n    59→    \"topics\": [\"coding-agents\", \"reverse-engineering\", \"ai-assisted-programming\", \"generative-ai\"],\n    60→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n    61→  },\n    62→  {\n    63→    \"title\": \"Who's Afraid of Chinese Models? - Proposal for AI data fair use and distillation rights\",\n    64→    \"description\": \"Ben Thompson proposes that the U.S. should pass a law making training data collection fair use and barring terms of service that forbid distillation. Also discusses Alibaba's Qwen 3.8 Max release and Xi Jinping's speech encouraging open source collaboration.\",\n    65→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Ben Thompson)\",\n    66→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    67→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    68→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-20\",\n    69→    \"topics\": [\"ai-ethics\", \"ai-in-china\", \"llms\", \"training-data\", \"qwen\", \"llm-release\"],\n    70→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n    71→  },\n    72→  {\n    73→    \"title\": \"Sam Altman's 2022 email about discouraging open models revealed in Musk v. Altman\",\n    74→    \"description\": \"Revelations from Musk v. Altman lawsuit show Sam Altman's 2022 strategy to release a GPT-3 class model that runs locally on consumer hardware to discourage others from releasing similar models and make it harder for new efforts to get funded.\",\n    75→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    76→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    77→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    78→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-20\",\n    79→    \"topics\": [\"ai-ethics\", \"sam-altman\", \"generative-ai\", \"openai\"],\n    80→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n    81→  },\n    82→  {\n    83→    \"title\": \"AI Mania Is Eviscerating Global Decision-Making\",\n    84→    \"description\": \"Nik Suresh reports on AI mania overwhelming large companies, including anecdotes about executives with no AI experience creating AI strategies, engineers gaming token leaderboards by having AI rewrite repos in Zig, and vendors unwilling to question customer claims of 100x productivity gains to avoid losing contracts.\",\n    85→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Nik Suresh)\",\n    86→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    87→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    88→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-19\",\n    89→    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"ai-ethics\", \"ai-misuse\"],\n    90→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n    91→  },\n    92→  {\n    93→    \"title\": \"Claude Code now using Bun written in Rust\",\n    94→    \"description\": \"Investigation confirming Claude Code v2.1.181+ uses the Rust port of Bun (Bun v1.4.0), with 563 Rust source files found in the binary. The Rust version has been released as Bun canary.\",\n    95→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    96→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    97→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    98→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-19\",\n    99→    \"topics\": [\"bun\", \"rust\", \"anthropic\", \"claude-code\"],\n   100→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   101→  },\n   102→  {\n   103→    \"title\": \"SQLite Query Explainer tool built with 