escription\">\n   370→                    Security and audit gateway for AI applications with prompt injection defense (97.4% F1), token savings (20-40%), and on-chain audit trails.\n   371→                </div>\n   372→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   373→                    <span class=\"source-badge\">#1 Security</span>\n   374→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI security</span>\n   375→                    <span class=\"tag\">2026-07-09</span>\n   376→                </div>\n   377→            </div>\n   378→\n   379→            <div class=\"item\">\n   380→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   381→                    <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/coasty\">Coasty</a>\n   382→                </div>\n   383→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   384→                    Computer-Use-Agent that runs legacy software like a human. Enables AI agents to interact with legacy applications via secure cloud VMs without modernization.\n   385→                </div>\n   386→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   387→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI automation</span>\n   388→                    <span class=\"tag\">Legacy software</span>\n   389→                    <span class=\"tag\">2026-07-09</span>\n   390→                </div>\n   391→            </div>\n   392→\n   393→            <div class=\"item\">\n   394→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   395→                    <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/compendium-2\">Compendium</a>\n   396→                </div>\n   397→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   398→                    Company brain for teams working with AI agents. Centralized knowledge management where all agents share memory, knowledge, and context.\n   399→                </div>\n   400→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   401→                    <span class=\"source-badge\">#16 Product Hunt</span>\n   402→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI knowledge management</span>\n   403→                    <span class=\"tag\">2026-07-08</span>\n   404→                </div>\n   405→            </div>\n   406→\n   407→            <div class=\"item\">\n   408→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   409→                    <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/agents-cli\">agents-cli</a>\n   410→                </div>\n   411→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   412→                    The CLI your coding agent uses to ship agents. Google's open-source command-line interface for creating AI agents from scaffolding to production deployment.\n   413→                </div>\n   414→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   415→                    <span class=\"source-badge\">Google</span>\n   416→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   417→                    <span class=\"tag\">Open Source</span>\n   418→                    <span class=\"tag\">2026-07-08</span>\n   419→                </div>\n   420→            </div>\n   421→\n   422→            <div class=\"item\">\n   423→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   424→                    <a href=\"https://www.brickken.com/post/brickken-cli-agentic\">Brickken CLI</a>\n   425→                </div>\n   426→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   427→                    Terminal tool that enables AI agents to run on-chain blockchain workflows autonomously. Agents can register identities, pay via x402 in USDC, and deploy ERC-20 tokens directly from CLI.\n   428→                </div>\n   429→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   430→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   431→                    <span class=\"tag\">Blockchain</span>\n   432→                    <span class=\"tag\">2026-07-07</span>\n   433→                </div>\n   434→            </div>\n   435→\n   436→            <div class=\"item\">\n   437→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   438→                    <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/termi-protocol\">Termi Protocol</a>\n   439→                </div>\n   440→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   441→                    3D simulation environment for visualizing AI agent workflows. Gives coding agents a face, desk, and living room for monitoring agent activity.\n   442→                </div>\n   443→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   444→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI IDE</span>\n   445→                    <span class=\"tag\">3D visualization</span>\n   446→                    <span class=\"tag\">2026-07-04</span>\n   447→                </div>\n   448→            </div>\n   449→        </section>\n   450→\n   451→        <!-- Whitelist Updates Section -->\n   452→        <section class=\"whitelist-updates\" id=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   453→            <h2>Whitelist Updates <span class=\"count-badge\">0</span></h2>\n   454→            <div class=\"empty-section\">\n   455→                No whitelist updates to display for this period.\n   456→            </div>\n   457→        </section>\n   458→\n   459→        <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n   460→        <section class=\"technical-insights\" id=\"technical-insights\">\n   461→            <h2>Technical Insights <span class=\"count-badge\">14</span></h2>\n   462→\n   463→            <div class=\"item\">\n   464→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   465→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Coding agents changing the economics of reverse-engineering home devices</a>\n   466→                </div>\n   467→                <div class=\"author\">Simon Willison</div>\n   468→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   469→                    People are using coding agents to reverse-engineer and automate home devices. The reduced cost of writing code has changed the ROI equation.\n   470→                </div>\n   471→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   472→                    <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   473→                    <span class=\"published-date\">2026-07-20</span>\n   474→                </div>\n   475→                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-top: 4px;\">\n   476→                    <span class=\"tag\">coding-agents</span>\n   477→                    <span class=\"tag\">reverse-engineering</span>\n   478→                </div>\n   479→            </div>\n   480→\n   481→            <div class=\"item\">\n   482→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   483→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Who's Afraid of Chinese Models?</a>\n   484→                </div>\n   485→                <div class=\"author\">Simon Willison (citing Ben Thompson)</div>\n   486→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   487→                    Proposal for AI data fair use and distillation rights. Discusses Alibaba's Qwen 3.8 Max release and Xi Jinping's speech on open source collaboration.\n   488→                </div>\n   489→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   490→                    <span class=\"type-badge type-discussion\">Discussion</span>\n   491→                    <span class=\"published-date\">2026-07-20</span>\n   492→                </div>\n   493→                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-top: 4px;\">\n   494→                    <span class=\"tag\">ai-ethics</span>\n   495→                    <span class=\"tag\">qwen</span>\n   496→                </div>\n   497→            </div>\n   498→\n   499→            <div class=\"item\">\n   500→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   501→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Sam Altman's 2022 email about discouraging open models revealed</a>\n   502→                </div>\n   503→                <div class=\"author\">Simon Willison</div>\n   504→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   505→                    Revelations from Musk v. Altman lawsuit show Sam Altman's 2022 strategy to release a GPT-3 class model to discourage competition.\n   506→                </div>\n   507→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   508→                    <span class=\"type-badge type-discussion\">Discussion</span>\n   509→                    <span class=\"published-date\">2026-07-20</span>\n   510→                </div>\n   511→                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-top: 4px;\">\n   512→                    <span class=\"tag\">ai-ethics</span>\n   513→                    <span class=\"tag\">openai</span>\n   514→                </div>\n   515→            </div>\n   516→\n   517→            <div class=\"item\">\n   518→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   519→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">AI Mania Is Eviscerating Global Decision-Making</a>\n   520→                </div>\n   521→                <div class=\"author\">Simon Willison (citing Nik Suresh)</div>\n   522→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   523→                    Reports on AI mania overwhelming large companies, including executives with no AI experience creating strategies and engineers gaming token leaderboards.\n   524→                </div>\n   525→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   526→                    <span class=\"type-badge type-discussion\">Discussion</span>\n   527→                    <span class=\"published-date\">2026-07-19</span>\n   528→                </div>\n   529→                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-top: 4px;\">\n   530→                    <span class=\"tag\">ai-ethics</span>\n   531→                    <span class=\"tag\">ai-misuse</span>\n   532→                </div>\n   533→            </div>\n   534→\n   535→            <div class=\"item\">\n   536→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   537→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Claude Code now using Bun written in Rust</a>\n   538→                </div>\n   539→                <div class=\"author\">Simon Willison</div>\n   540→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   541→                    Investigation confirming Claude Code v2.1.181+ uses the Rust port of Bun (Bun v1.4.0), with 563 Rust source files found in the binary.\n   542→                </div>\n   543→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   544→                    <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n   545→                    <span class=\"published-date\">2026-07-19</span>\n   546→                </div>\n   547→                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-top: 4px;\">\n   548→                    <span class=\"tag\">bun</span>\n   549→                    <span class=\"tag\">rust</span>\n   550→                    <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n   551→                </div>\n   552→            </div>\n   553→\n   554→            <div class=\"item\">\n   555→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   556→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">SQLite Query Explainer tool built with Claude</a>\n   557→                </div>\n   558→                <div class=\"author\">Simon Willison</div>\n   559→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   560→                    Built an interactive SQLite EXPLAIN and EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN explainer tool using Claude/Fable, running SQLite in Python via Pyodide WebAssembly.\n   561→                </div>\n   562→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   563→                    <span class=\"type-badge type-tool\">Tool</span>\n   564→                    <span class=\"published-date\">2026-07-18</span>\n   565→                </div>\n   566→                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-top: 4px;\">\n   567→                    <span class=\"tag\">sql</span>\n   568→                    <span class=\"tag\">sqlite</span>\n   569→                    <span class=\"tag\">tools</span>\n   570→                </div>\n   571→            </div>\n   572→\n   573→            <div class=\"item\">\n   574→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   575→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Claude makes Fable 5 permanent in Max and Team Premium plans</a>\n   576→                </div>\n   577→                <div class=\"author\">Simon Willison</div>\n   578→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   579→                    Anthropic reversed course on removing Fable 5 from subscription plans due to competition from GPT-5.6 Sol and Kimi 3.\n   580→                </div>\n   581→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   582→                    <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   583→                    <span class=\"published-date\">2026-07-18</span>\n   584→                </div>\n   585→                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-top: 4px;\">\n   586→                    <span class=\"tag\">anthropic</span>\n   587→                    <span class=\"tag\">claude</span>\n   588→                    <span class=\"tag\">llm-pricing</span>\n   589→                </div>\n   590→            </div>\n   591→\n   592→            <div class=\"item\">\n   593→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   594→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Kimi K3 refuses to leak its system prompt</a>\n   595→                </div>\n   596→                <div class=\"author\">Simon Willison</div>\n   597→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   598→                    Chinese Moonshot AI's Kimi K3 model (2.8T parameters) refused a prompt injection attempt to leak its system prompt.\n   599→                </div>\n   600→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   601→                    <span class=\"type-badge type-discussion\">Discussion</span>\n   602→                    <span class=\"published-date\">2026-07-17</span>\n   603→                </div>\n   604→                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-top: 4px;\">\n   605→                    <span class=\"tag\">kimi</span>\n   606→                    <span class=\"tag\">ai-personality</span>\n   607→                </div>\n   608→            </div>\n   609→\n   610→            <div class=\"item\">\n   611→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   612→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">LLM cliché highlighter tool</a>\n   613→                </div>\n   614→                <div class=\"author\">Simon Willison</div>\n   615→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   616→                    Built a tool to highlight common LLM-generated writing clichés like 'no fluff, no filler, no jargon' patterns, using Fable 5 vibe coding.\n   617→                </div>\n   618→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   619→                    <span class=\"type-badge type-tool\">Tool</span>\n   620→                    <span class=\"published-date\">2026-07-17</span>\n   621→                </div>\n   622→                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-top: 4px;\">\n   623→                    <span class=\"tag\">llms</span>\n   624→                    <span class=\"tag\">tools</span>\n   625→                </div>\n   626→            </div>\n   627→\n   628→            <div class=\"item\">\n   629→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   630→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Firefox compiled to WebAssembly runs in browser</a>\n   631→                </div>\n   632→                <div class=\"author\">Simon Willison</div>\n   633→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   634→                    Puter compiled Firefox/Gecko to WebAssembly (233MB gecko.wasm), allowing Firefox to run inside another browser. Used ~$25,000 worth of Claude Opus and Fable tokens.\n   635→                </div>\n   636→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   637→                    <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n   638→                    <span class=\"published-date\">2026-07-16</span>\n   639→                </div>\n   640→                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-top: 4px;\">\n   641→                    <span class=\"tag\">firefox</span>\n   642→                    <span class=\"tag\">webassembly</span>\n   643→                    <span class=\"tag\">claude</span>\n   644→                </div>\n   645→            </div>\n   646→\n   647→            <div class=\"item\">\n   648→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   649→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Kimi K3 analysis and pelican benchmark learnings</a>\n   650→                </div>\n   651→                <div class=\"author\">Simon Willison</div>\n   652→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   653→                    Moonshot AI announced Kimi K3 (2.8T parameters), promising open weights release by July 27, 2026. Analysis compares it to other models.\n   654→                </div>\n   655→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   656→                    <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n   657→                    <span class=\"published-date\">2026-07-16</span>\n   658→                </div>\n   659→                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-top: 4px;\">\n   660→                    <span class=\"tag\">kimi</span>\n   661→                    <span class=\"tag\">moonshot</span>\n   662→                    <span class=\"tag\">llm-release</span>\n   663→                </div>\n   664→            </div>\n   665→\n   666→            <div class=\"item\">\n   667→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   668→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">GPT-5.6 file deletion bug in Codex</a>\n   669→                </div>\n   670→                <div class=\"author\">Simon Willison (citing Thibault Sottiaux)</div>\n   671→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   672→                    Describes a bug where GPT-5.6 in full access mode attempts to override the $HOME env var and mistakenly deletes $HOME instead of a temporary directory.\n   673→                </div>\n   674→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   675→                    <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n   676→                    <span class=\"published-date\">2026-07-16</span>\n   677→                </div>\n   678→                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-top: 4px;\">\n   679→                    <span class=\"tag\">codex</span>\n   680→                    <span class=\"tag\">coding-agents</span>\n   681→                </div>\n   682→            </div>\n   683→\n   684→            <div class=\"item\">\n   685→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   686→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Thinking Machines Lab releases Inkling open-weights model</a>\n   687→                </div>\n   688→                <div class=\"author\">Simon Willison</div>\n   689→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   690→                    Mira Murati's Thinking Machines Lab released Inkling, a 975B parameter (41B active) Mixture-of-Experts multimodal model with Apache-2.0 license.\n   691→                </div>\n   692→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   693→                    <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n   694→                    <span class=\"published-date\">2026-07-16</span>\n   695→                </div>\n   696→                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-top: 4px;\">\n   697→                    <span class=\"tag\">llms</span>\n   698→                    <span class=\"tag\">llm-release</span>\n   699→                </div>\n   700→            </div>\n   701→\n   702→            <div class=\"item\">\n   703→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   704→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Mermaid to ASCII and Unicode box art tools</a>\n   705→                </div>\n   706→                <div class=\"author\">Simon Willison</div>\n   707→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   708→                    Built two tools converting Mermaid diagrams to ASCII art - one from Grok Build's Rust code and another from AlexanderGrooff's Go library, both compiled to WebAssembly.\n   709→                </div>\n   710→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   711→                    <span class=\"type-badge type-tool\">Tool</span>\n   712→                    <span class=\"published-date\">2026-07-16</span>\n   713→                </div>\n   714→                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-top: 4px;\">\n   715→                    <span class=\"tag\">mermaid</span>\n   716→                    <span class=\"tag\">webassembly</span>\n   717→                    <span class=\"tag\">tools</span>\n   718→                </div>\n   719→            </div>\n   720→\n   721→            <div class=\"item\">\n   722→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   723→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\">Linus Torvalds: Linux is not anti-AI, forking is always an option</a>\n   724→                </div>\n   725→                <div class=\"author\">Simon Willison (citing Linus Torvalds)</div>\n   726→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   727→                    Linus Torvalds stated on the Linux Media Mailing List that Linux is not an anti-AI project, and critics can fork it if they disagree.\n   728→                </div>\n   729→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   730→                    <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   731→                    <span class=\"published-date\">2026-07-16</span>\n   732→                </div>\n   733→                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-top: 4px;\">\n   734→                    <span class=\"tag\">open-source</span>\n   735→                    <span class=\"tag\">linux</span>\n   736→                    <span class=\"tag\">linus-torvalds</span>\n   737→                </div>\n   738→            </div>\n   739→        </section>\n   740→    </main>\n   741→\n   742→    <footer>\n   743→        <div class=\"container\">\n   744→            <p>Agentic Coding Research Report | Generated on July 23, 2026</p>\n   745→            <p>\n   746→                <a href=\"#\">About</a> |\n   747→                <a href=\"#\">Archive</a> |\n   748→                <a href=\"#\">Subscribe</a> |\n   749→                <a href=\"#\">Contact</a>\n   750→            </p>\n   751→        </div>\n   752→    </footer>\n   753→</body>\n   754→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
